WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.180
Now that the X-Men movie rights are finally
back in Marvel's hands, MCU fans are running

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.220
wild with speculation as to which mutants
might show up in the franchise first.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.870
From A-list icons to ambitious wildcards,
these are the X-Men who most deserve a place

00:00:13.870 --> 00:00:15.680
in the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:20.520
2018's Black Panther was more than just a
huge money-maker for Marvel Studios.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:26.140
Sure, it grossed a cool $1.3 billion at the
box office, but it also kicked the franchise

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:30.920
up a notch by introducing a genuinely compelling
villain, a thought-provoking premise, and

00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:33.540
arguably the best MCU romance to date.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:39.280
But while Lupita Nyong'o's and Chadwick Boseman
shared some undeniable chemistry as Nakia

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:44.780
and T'Challa, the King of Wakanda actually
married someone completely different in the

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:46.920
comics: Ororo Munroe, also known as Storm.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:53.220
In comic lore, Ororo and T'Challa first met
as children, when she used her weather-manipulating

00:00:53.229 --> 00:00:56.539
powers to save the young prince from a kidnapping
in Africa.

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.480
The two young lovers remained close through
the years, eventually marrying in 2006.

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:05.600
Although they eventually had their marriage
annulled after the events of the Avengers

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:10.940
vs. X-Men story-line in 2012, they still shared
a good six years of marital bliss.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:17.030
With Black Panther 2 officially slated for
release on May 6, 2022, Marvel has the perfect

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:20.820
opportunity to introduce Storm while staying
true to the source material.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:26.620
Back in February 2018, Comicbook.com asked
director Ryan Coogler about a potential Storm

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.100
sighting in a future sequel.

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:28.940
He replied:

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:32.780
"I don't know enough about that acquisition
to even talk about it [...] if it's something

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:36.990
that goes through, I can't think of better
hands for those characters to be in than Kevin

00:01:36.990 --> 00:01:37.480
Feige."

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:42.860
With the rights finally in hand, a Storm may
indeed be brewing for Black Panther 2.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.700
He may not have been part of the original
comics team, but these days it's hard to imagine

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.400
the X-Men without Wolverine.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.900
Hugh Jackman played the iconic role for 17
years and nine movies before finally deciding

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:59.860
to hang up his claws after 2017's wildly successful
swan song, Logan.

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.640
And while Wolverine might be pivotal to the
X-Men universe, his first major comic book

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.700
appearance didn't have anything to do with
them.

00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:12.890
Logan's first outing was in 1974's Incredible
Hulk #181, in which he first fought the Jade

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:18.020
Giant - yes, he appeared in the last panel
of the prior issue but we said “fought”

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.040
- so relax.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.420
What could this mean for the MCU?

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:25.190
Obviously, you could make the argument that
it would be fitting to introduce Wolverine

00:02:25.190 --> 00:02:29.660
in a future Hulk project, either on Disney+
or on the silver screen.

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:34.190
Given that Mark Ruffalo's Bruce Banner lived
through the events of Endgame, you'd have

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:37.700
to assume that Bruce will show up in the MCU
again, too, right?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:42.300
So what better way to bring him back than
to have him square off against an ultra-powerful

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:43.520
threat like Wolverine?

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:48.640
Most MCU fans were pretty excited to hear
that Tom Hiddleston's Loki would be getting

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.660
his own streaming series on Disney+.

00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:55.740
And given that Endgame's alternate-reality
version of Loki is still hellbent on world

00:02:55.740 --> 00:03:00.500
domination, it sounds like the ambitious trickster
will be getting back to his villainous ways.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.420
“Surprise.”

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:08.000
In the comics, Loki once captured one of the
original X-Men, Iceman, to try and use his

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:10.420
freezing powers to make his Frost Giants stronger.

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.720
Given that the MCU's Loki is also portrayed
as the heir to Jotunheim, the land of the

00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:19.940
Frost Giants, it's possible that Hiddleston's
iteration of the character will try this ploy,

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:20.440
too.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:25.000
Bobby Drake's Iceman, one of the founding
members of the X-Men, has seen his popularity

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:28.900
grow throughout the years, but that's not
just because of his incredible, ice-powered

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:29.400
abilities.

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:35.150
In 2015, he came out as gay, making him an
important figure for representation in comics

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:38.320
the kind of representation that's long overdue
in the MCU.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:43.420
Of course, tying your hopes to the God of
Mischief is usually a fool's errand and only

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:46.480
time will tell what Loki has up his sleeve
for his own series.

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:52.340
Comic book fans might know that Carol Danvers
has a seriously twisted history with longtime

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.360
X-Men member Rogue, whose absorption powers
made her one of the X-Men's most formidable

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:57.860
members.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.980
Their beef began when Rogue, while working
with Mystique and the Brotherhood of Evil

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:07.580
Mutants, drained Carol's powers and memories,
stealing her powers of flight and super-strength.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:12.440
Although Carol eventually reclaimed her identity
and abilities, she and Rogue have remained

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.280
fierce rivals throughout the years.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:20.060
Of course, the Fox version of Rogue never
got to do anything this cool, and that's because

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:24.260
Fox didn't have the rights to Carol Danvers
so they obviously couldn't give her that backstory

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:24.960
in the first place.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.560
Now that Marvel has reclaimed their mutants,
however, it's entirely possible that fans

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:33.540
might finally get a comic-accurate version
of Rogue in the MCU.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.700
And where better to debut her than in Captain
Marvel 2?

00:04:37.280 --> 00:04:38.280
Poor Channing Tatum.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:43.360
For years, the Magic Mike star has been vying
for a Gambit movie with himself in the titular

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:43.920
role.

00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:47.580
Sadly, it's looking more and more like that
film is never going to happen.

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.220
But maybe there's another way Tatum can play
the role of the Ragin' Cajun.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:57.080
One of the many streaming series on the upcoming
Disney+ roster is Hawkeye, a show focusing

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:58.940
on Jeremy Renner's archer Avenger.

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:04.060
Despite his involvement in the Avengers movies,
Renner's Clint Barton isn't really perceived

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:06.160
as an A-list MCU character.

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:11.840
As such, his series isn't quite as hotly-anticipated
as, say, Loki or WandaVision.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:16.360
Perhaps a great way to inject some much needed
pizzazz into Hawkeye would be to give Channing

00:05:16.360 --> 00:05:19.860
Tatum what he's always wanted: a chance to
play Gambit.

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:25.240
The two heroes have crossed paths in the comics,
so it's not an entirely unprecedented move.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:28.940
They both have somewhat similar powers, too,
with Barton's bow precision being comparable

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:32.100
to Gambit's explosive card-throwing accuracy.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.300
And whether you have them at odds or teaming
up, it does seem like a great way to lend

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.480
some hype to a show that could probably use
it.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:43.740
One of the many lasting impacts of Endgame
is that Gamora, longtime member of the Guardians

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:47.100
of the Galaxy, is no longer the same character
fans have grown to love.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:51.580
Her whole existence was thrown upside-down
due to the one-two punch of her sacrifice

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:55.680
for the Soul Stone at the hands of Thanos
and the repercussions of the Avengers' time

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:56.180
heist.

00:05:56.660 --> 00:06:01.940
Now, the MCU is home to a Gamora who is alive
but who hasn't gone on the journey fans have

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:05.400
witnessed, with no memories of her time with
the Guardians or with Peter Quill.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:09.740
But don't cry for Star Lord just yet because
there could be a new flame appearing in his

00:06:09.740 --> 00:06:10.420
near future.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:14.920
Enter Kitty Pryde, the spunky, wall-phasing
member of the X-Men.

00:06:14.940 --> 00:06:18.640
In recent years, Pryde has developed a strong
bond with Peter Quill.

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:22.950
They first met when the X-Men and Guardians
teamed up on a space mission involving the

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.340
Shi'ar alien race.

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:29.419
After completing the mission, the two lovebirds
remained close, giving the term "long-distance

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:30.820
relationship" a whole new meaning.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:35.160
Although Fox's X-Men movies did include the
Kitty Pryde character, you could argue that

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:38.260
her minor role in that universe didn't really
do her justice.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:43.020
This is a character who has done some seriously
impressive things on the page, including traveling

00:06:43.020 --> 00:06:44.980
through time and even killing Wolverine.

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:50.660
So here's hoping a more comic-accurate Pryde
makes her debut in the MCU sometime soon.

00:06:51.100 --> 00:06:56.260
James Wan's Aquaman hit theaters in 2018,
dominating the worldwide box office with a

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:59.120
gross of a whopping $1.1 billion.

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:03.760
Now, for seemingly the first time in the past
ten years, Marvel is staring at an opportunity

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:09.330
to take a page from the DCEU's playbook and
try to capitalize on the musclebound fish-men

00:07:09.330 --> 00:07:09.820
craze.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:14.800
One of Marvel's first-ever characters was
Namor the Sub-Mariner [NAY-mor the SUB-mair-ihn-uhr],

00:07:14.810 --> 00:07:15.900
King of Atlantis.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.919
It's been more than 80 years since his on-page
debut, and although he has fought both for

00:07:20.919 --> 00:07:25.000
and against the heroes of the Marvel Universe
during that time, he is widely considered

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:25.680
a good guy.

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:30.620
He became an official member of the Avengers
in 1985, but more recently, he joined the

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:33.840
Uncanny X-Men in their 2009 comic run.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:38.560
Namor's affiliation with the X-Men has actually
earned him a powerful rival in the past ten

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:41.020
years: Wakanda's King T'Challa.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:47.020
During the epic Avengers vs. X-Men comic event,
a Phoenix force-corrupted Namor even went

00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:52.700
so far as to attack Wakanda with his Atlantean
army, bringing great destruction to the African

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:53.200
nation.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:58.100
Should Marvel choose to bring their "first
mutant" into the MCU, Black Panther 2 could

00:07:58.110 --> 00:07:59.699
be a great place to do so.

00:07:59.699 --> 00:08:05.050
There was even a potential Easter egg in Avengers:
Endgame that fans believe hinted to his arrival,

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.250
with Okoye mentioning a sub-oceanic earthquake
off the coast of Africa.

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.660
"It was a mild subduction under the African
plate.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:13.820
“Do we have a visual how are we handling
it?”

00:08:14.240 --> 00:08:14.980
“Net.

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:17.100
It’s an earthquake under the ocean."

00:08:17.700 --> 00:08:21.940
Fingers crossed for a clash of kings in T'Challa's
next solo outing.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:27.300
When Jubilee joined the X-Men at the dawn
of the 1990's, she became one of the youngest

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:28.940
members of the team's roster.

00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:34.320
A mutant capable of shooting firework-like
energy plasmoids out of her hands, the young

00:08:34.330 --> 00:08:39.029
Chinese-American heroine quickly became a
fan favorite due to her quirky personality

00:08:39.029 --> 00:08:40.459
and dazzling appeal.

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:45.140
However, after a run-in with a certain foe,
she became much more than just a mutant.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:49.879
In the Curse of the Mutants crossover event
in 2011, the X-Men found themselves going

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:51.320
toe-to-toe with vampires.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:52.500
Yeah, vampires.

00:08:52.940 --> 00:08:58.480
Anyways, in the comics, Jubilee was bitten
by Xarus, the son of Dracula, and actually

00:08:58.480 --> 00:09:02.940
became a vampire herself, making use of a
special amulet that allowed her to walk in

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:03.440
the sun.

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:08.000
Why should a vampiric mutant earn an early
invitation to the MCU?

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:13.020
Because the day-walker himself, Blade, is
coming soon to a theater near you.

00:09:13.029 --> 00:09:19.009
If Feige and company add a fan-favorite like
Jubes to Oscar winner Mahershala Ali's MCU

00:09:19.009 --> 00:09:21.220
debut, the hype will be unreal.

00:09:21.420 --> 00:09:23.400
Talk about an explosive opening weekend.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:28.660
Any mutant fan will know that Scarlet Witch
and Quicksilver are the biological children

00:09:28.660 --> 00:09:34.559
of X-Men super villain Magneto, but you might
not know that the twins actually have a secret,

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:39.840
lesser known sibling: Lorna Dane, the green-haired
mutant also known as Polaris.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:45.140
In the comics, Polaris shares similar abilities
to those of her father, being able to manipulate

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:47.280
magnetic fields and lift metals.

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:51.900
Although she has had her fair share of conflicts
with both heroes and villains, she eventually

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:55.800
joined the X-Men after they saved her from
the mutant-hunting Sentinels.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:10:02.200
Although Emma Dumont already portrayed her
on FX's X-Men-affiliated series The Gifted,

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.980
there's no reason why the MCU couldn't adapt
their own version of the character.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:11.380
Should Disney+'s WandaVision choose dive into
more of Wanda's origin story, discovering

00:10:11.380 --> 00:10:15.520
a secretly gifted half-sister like Polaris
could make for a juicy plot twist.

